.TH PDRIVE 1 "November 2026" "PDrive for Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdrive \- command-line tool of PDrive for Linux, an unofficial Proton Drive client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdrive
.BR login " | " logout " | " status " | " selftest
.br
.B pdrive ls
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.BR pdrive " " keep\-offline " | " free\-up\-space
.IR PATH ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdrive
signs in to and out of a Proton account and lists folders of
.IR "My files" .
The drive itself is mounted by
.BR pdrived (1),
usually run by
.BR pdrive-app (1).
.PP
PDrive for Linux is an unofficial third-party client. It is not affiliated with,
or endorsed by, Proton AG.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B login
Sign in through the web browser and store the session in the Secret Service
keyring (oo7, GNOME Keyring, KWallet, KeePassXC...).
.TP
.BI "ls [" PATH ]
List a folder of
.I My files
(for example
.BR "pdrive ls Documents/Invoices" ).
Without
.IR PATH ,
list the root.
.TP
.B logout
Revoke the session and remove it from the keyring.
.TP
.B status
Print
.B signed in
or
.BR "not signed in" .
.TP
.BI "keep\-offline " PATH ...
Keep the files or folders available offline (same action as the Nautilus and Dolphin
menus). Each
.I PATH
must be inside the mounted drive: the others are ignored with a message.
.TP
.BI "free\-up\-space " PATH ...
Free the local space used by the files or folders (they stay in the drive).
.PP
.RS
Both commands talk to the running daemon. When it is not running, or when no
.I PATH
is in the drive, they print the reason, show a desktop notification, and exit with status 1.
They are what the COSMIC Files context-menu actions run.
.RE
.TP
.B selftest
Check the bridge with the SDK library without network access.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B status
exits with 0 if a session is stored, 1 otherwise. Any command exits with 2 when
the arguments are not understood, and with a non-zero status on failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PDRIVE_VERBOSE
When set, log HTTP requests and SDK debug messages.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pdrive/config.toml
Settings (see
.BR pdrived (1)).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdrive-app (1),
.BR pdrived (1)
.PP
